    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Summary\n\n`mergePR` in `packages/mobile/lib/api.ts:773-775` posts to `/api/v1/prs/{id}/merge` with no request body. The endpoint requires `prUrl` and `expectedHeadSha`, so the call can only return 400. Nothing calls it today, so it is latent, but it will bite whoever adds a merge button.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```\n# exactly what the helper sends\ncurl -i -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:3001/api/v1/prs/2/merge\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe helper sends a `MergePRRequest`, or it is removed until something needs it.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n```\nHTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\n{\"error\":\"bad_request\",\"code\":\"INVALID_JSON\",\"message\":\"Invalid JSON body\"}\n```\n\nThe store wraps this in a `merge` action (`packages/mobile/lib/store.tsx:454-461`) that also has no caller, so both are dead code right now.\n\nWorth knowing before someone wires a button to it: the daemon refuses to merge unless CI is passing and a review is approved. `MergeReadiness.ReadyToMerge` in `backend/internal/domain/pr.go:226-238` treats unknown CI as not ready. I hit that on a test repo with no checks at all. The PR card in the app read Mergeable, and a correctly formed merge call came back 422 `PR_PRECONDITIONS_UNMET`. So a merge button needs a disabled state with a reason, not a request that fails.\n\n### AO version\n\n0.12.11-nightly.202609011721 (packaged app); mobile from origin/main d6350bc47\n\n### Environment\n\nmacOS 26.5 arm64\n\n### Logs / extra context\n\n```shell\n$ curl -i -s -X POST $AO/prs/2/merge\nHTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request\n{\"error\":\"bad_request\",\"code\":\"INVALID_JSON\",\"message\":\"Invalid JSON body\"}\n\n# correctly formed, on a repo with no CI checks:\n$ curl -s -X POST $AO/prs/2/merge -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n    -d '{\"prUrl\":\"https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/pull/2\",\"expectedHeadSha\":\"<sha>\"}'\n422 {\"error\":\"unprocessable\",\"code\":\"PR_PRECONDITIONS_UNMET\"}\n```\n\n### Before submitting\n\n- [X] I searched existing issues for duplicates\n- [X] I removed secrets / tokens from logs and screenshots\n",
